Night blindness is the inability to see in dim light or at night. It is due to disorder of the cells in the retina that are responsible for vision in dim light and can result from dietary deficiency of vitamin A (retinol).
\(\begin{array}{|l|l|l|}
\hline \text { Name } & \text { Sources } & \text { Effect of deficiency } \\
\hline \begin{array}{l}
\text { Vit. C } \\
\text { (Ascorbic acid) }
\end{array} & \begin{array}{l}
\text { Lemon, orange and } \\
\text { other citrus fruits, } \\
\text { tomatoes, green } \\
\text { vegetables, potatoes, } \\
\text { carrots, pepper etc. }
\end{array} & \begin{array}{l}
\text { Scurvy (also called } \\
\text { sailor's disease) is } \\
\text { characterised by wound } \\
\text {-healing and growth } \\
\text { retardation etc. }
\end{array} \\
\hline \begin{array}{l}
\text { Vit. D } \\
\text { (Ergocalciferol } \\
\text { and } \\
\text { Cholecalciferol) }
\end{array} & \begin{array}{l}
\text { Synthesized in skin } \\
\text { cells in sunlight from } \\
\text { 7-dehydrocholesterol } \\
\text { (i.e. provitamin } \mathrm{D}_3 \text { ), } \\
\text { also found in butter, } \\
\text { liver, kidneys, egg } \\
\text { yolk, fish, oil, etc. }
\end{array} & \begin{array}{l}
\text { Rickets, a disorder of } \\
\text { children of 6 months to } \\
\text { 2years, and osteomalacia, } \\
\text { a disorder of adults. }
\end{array} \\
\hline \begin{array}{l}
\text { Vit. E } \\
\text { (Tocopherol) }
\end{array} & \begin{array}{l}
\text { Green vegetables, } \\
\text { oils, egg yolk, } \\
\text { wheat, animal } \\
\text { tissues }
\end{array} & \begin{array}{l}
\text { Reversible sterility in } \\
\text { female. In male causes } \\
\text { atrophy of spermatogenic } \\
\text { tubules of testes. }
\end{array} \\
\hline
\end{array}\)
